## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ_y3eiW8AAVEGD?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536/cobi%5Fbean/article/2062644695776248096/media/2062634189262876672) Hermes Desktop Masterclass...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>cobi</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/cobi_bean">@cobi_bean</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536">http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536">http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ_y3eiW8AAVEGD?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536/cobi%5Fbean/article/2062644695776248096/media/2062634189262876672)<br/>Hermes Desktop Masterclass<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2050065487942369280/gRHqAkQp_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536/cobi%5Fbean)<br/>[cobi](http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536/cobi%5Fbean)<br/>[@cobi\_bean](http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536/cobi%5Fbean)<br/>·<br/>16h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow cobi\_bean<br/>9<br/>20<br/>175<br/>[122K](http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536/cobi%5Fbean/status/2062644695776248096/analytics)<br/>## <br/>i’ve been using Hermes mostly through Telegram for almost 4 months.<br/>which is sick - because i can talk to my agent from anywhere; phone laptop walking around whatever // wherever. <br/>but after using the new Hermes Desktop app, the thing that clicked for me is pretty simple:<br/>&gt; chat (TG, WhatsApp, Discord, etc...) is a great way to talk to your agent. desktop is where you actually see the system around it.<br/>that’s the part i think people are going to underrate.<br/>## <br/>Hermes Desktop gives your agent a home base.<br/>you can see tools.you can see skills.you can see crons.you can see sessions.you can switch profiles.you can see live agent runs.you can see memory/context settings.you can connect local or remote gateways.<br/>if you’ve been operating through Telegram, Discord, WhatsApp, texts, or any other chat surface, this is a massive upgrade.<br/>the main character here is visibility.<br/># <br/>the killer feature: session continuity<br/>the first thing that felt kind of magical:<br/>i could start with my Hermes agent from my phone, then open Hermes Desktop and pick up the same session there.<br/>same agent.same sessions.same skills.same memory.same config.<br/>the conversation doesn’t disappear into a messaging app scrollback.<br/>you can start something on Telegram, then move into Desktop when you need more control, more visibility, or just more screen space.<br/>you can also go the other way: start something in Desktop, leave halfway through, then pick up that same session on your phone in Telegram.<br/>that matters a lot if you actually use agents for work.<br/>because a real agent session is rarely just “send one message, get one answer.”<br/>it turns into:<br/>* checking what happened<br/>* continuing old context<br/>* seeing what tools fired<br/>* finding artifacts<br/>* managing settings<br/>* switching models<br/>* watching context usage<br/>* dealing with approvals<br/>* jumping between different agents/profiles<br/>that stuff is painful when everything is hidden behind chat.<br/>Desktop makes it visible.<br/>[![Square profile picture](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1816254738234761216/TX7TW-Mp_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536/NousResearch)<br/>Nous Research<br/>@NousResearch<br/>·<br/>[Jun 2](http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536/NousResearch/status/2061843507417944552)<br/>The next evolution of Hermes Agent is here! Introducing Hermes Desktop: everything you love about Hermes, now native on your machine. First demoed in Jensen's GTC keynote, it's now in public preview.<br/>![](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ0jlUAWsAEsYRd.jpg)<br/>1.1K<br/>2K<br/>12K<br/>[5.6M](http://x.com/i/article/2062531985239617536/NousResearch/status/2061843507417944552/analytics)<br/># <br/>the app feels like an agent command center<br/>when you open Hermes Desktop, the layout is familiar if you’ve used tools like Codex or Claude-style coding apps.<br/>sessions/chats on the side. main conversation in the middle. controls/settings around the edges.<br/>but the important thing is what it exposes.<br/>you’re not just staring at a chat box.<br/>you get a surface for the whole agent runtime.<br/>some of the stuff that stood out to me:<br/>## <br/>1\. agents view<br/>there’s an Agents button that shows your current/live agent runs and sub-agents.<br/>this is one of those featur</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 187 · 🔁 19 · 💬 9 · 🔖 538</p><p><a href="https://x.com/cobi_bean/status/2062644695776248096">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
