      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Startup Ideas Podcast (SIP) 🧃</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/startupideaspod">@startupideaspod</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416">http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416">http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKALodMbYAA81vW?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416/startupideaspod/article/2062662633472622784/media/2062661418995113984)<br/>OpenAI Codex: Build Apps That Work For You 24/7<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1955709395553124352/b_NlfUL__normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416/startupideaspod)<br/>[The Startup Ideas Podcast (SIP) ![🧃](https://abs.twimg.com/emoji/v2/svg/1f9c3.svg)](http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416/startupideaspod)<br/>[@startupideaspod](http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416/startupideaspod)<br/>·<br/>8h<br/>·<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow startupideaspod<br/>2<br/>3<br/>53<br/>[6.9K](http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416/startupideaspod/status/2062662633472622784/analytics)<br/>Codex shipped Sites.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKAMInnasAAApP7?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416/startupideaspod/article/2062662633472622784/media/2062661971548483584)<br/>I assumed it was a clunky Replit clone.<br/>Six prompts later, I had a startup board that updates itself.<br/>I used to run a web design agency. Back then I told clients one thing on repeat: a website is a living, breathing thing. You ship it, then it needs care every week.<br/>My own site proves the point. 158,000 people read my newsletter. When that climbs to 160,000, I open the file and edit it by hand.<br/>In 2026, an agent can carry that for me.<br/>The real difference<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKAMFUXaMAAjmUF?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416/startupideaspod/article/2062662633472622784/media/2062661914841460736)<br/>Replit and Lovable give you everything in one box. Editor, database, server, hosting, even a domain. Perfect when you want to type one prompt and walk away.<br/>Codex Sites asks more of you. It assumes you live in Codex and keep your context there. In return, it does something rare. It keeps building the app on its own.<br/>I built a Startup Ideas OS in six prompts<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKAMMCebQAAWgIi?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416/startupideaspod/article/2062662633472622784/media/2062662030298136576)<br/>The goal: a live board with five columns. Inbox, researching, validating, building, killed. Each card holds an idea, the buyer, the pain, proof, a next step, and a score.<br/>An internal tool I would actually use.<br/>Prompt 1\. Build the shell.Invoke it with <br/>[@sites](https://x.com/@sites)<br/>. It runs as a plugin. Ask for realistic sample data. Then add the five words that change everything: save for review, do not deploy. Left alone, it rushes to ship. That one line keeps the work in product mode.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKAMW_kasAAnSdi?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416/startupideaspod/article/2062662633472622784/media/2062662218496520192)<br/>Prompt 2\. Add memory.Codex Sites starts fresh each visit. Ask it to add persistent storage so ideas save between visits. The trick: tell it to show you the data model first, before it writes code. It came back with Cloudflare D1 as the store, one record type called ideas, and a clean list of actions. List, add, update, move, score, archive. Memory turns a demo into real software.<br/>Prompt 3\. Add safe actions.This is the part people sleep on. A safe action is an approved button. The agent calls named moves like add idea or update idea, and only those. Why it matters: I can sit in any Codex chat, spitball a startup idea, say add idea, and it lands on the live board through the one approved path.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKAMbU1aUAAVwto?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2062661069458620416/startupideaspod/article/2062662633472622784/media/2062662292924420096)<br/>Prompt 4\. Create a skill.Ask Codex to build a skil</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 67 · 🔁 1 · 💬 3 · 🔖 102</p><p><a href="https://x.com/startupideaspod/status/2062662633472622784">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
