## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ__ZKabkAA2NiA?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/dkundel/article/2062650378089594955/media/2062647962116001792) A guide to /goal ![🥅](https://abs.twimg.com/emoji/v2/svg/1f945.svg)...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>dominik kundel</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/dkundel">@dkundel</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392">http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392">http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ__ZKabkAA2NiA?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/dkundel/article/2062650378089594955/media/2062647962116001792)<br/>A guide to /goal ![🥅](https://abs.twimg.com/emoji/v2/svg/1f945.svg)<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2058062533496565760/Jcn_Jm9u_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/dkundel)<br/>[dominik kundel](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/dkundel)<br/>[@dkundel](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/dkundel)<br/>·<br/>3h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow dkundel<br/>12<br/>53<br/>474<br/>[104K](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/dkundel/status/2062650378089594955/analytics)<br/>We launched the goal mode (or /goal) as a way to help you have Codex drive towards a concrete outcome. When you set a goal Codex will continue to work until the goal is achieved, whether that takes hours or days. Some people have used Codex to work on a single goal for more than 120 hours.<br/>[![Square profile picture](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2022002720971096064/l3Kyt4qt_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/OpenAIDevs)<br/>OpenAI Developers<br/>![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1885410181409820672/ztsaR0JW_bigger.jpg)<br/>@OpenAIDevs<br/>·<br/>[May 21](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/OpenAIDevs/status/2057530209470210453)<br/>Replying to <br/>[@OpenAIDevs](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/OpenAIDevs)<br/>![🥅](https://abs.twimg.com/emoji/v2/svg/1f945.svg)/goal has graduated from an experiment—for tasks big and small, Codex gets your work done. Use goal mode in the Codex app, IDE Extension, or CLI to give Codex a specific milestone, and it will keep working until it gets there, even across hours or days. You can check in and<br/>Show more<br/>![](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HI3SW4jaEAEKG-C.jpg)<br/>46<br/>132<br/>1.3K<br/>[437K](http://x.com/i/article/2062645394719547392/OpenAIDevs/status/2057530209470210453/analytics)<br/>Goal mode is incredibly powerful, and there are a few things you can do to get the most out of it. Here are 7 things to keep in mind when you use /goal.<br/>## <br/>1\. Clear \*verifiable\* criteria<br/>The prompt you define when you activate goal mode might act as your initial prompt but more importantly it will act as your exit criteria for the goal. Codex will check after a turn whether the goal has been achieved or not. As a result your goal prompt should not be overly long and focus on a clear criteria on when the goal has been achieved.<br/>In most cases a good goal contains a clear number\* for the model to reach before the goal is considered complete. Good examples:<br/>1. "Reduce the build and deployment time by 30%."<br/>2. "Migrate this feature from TypeScript to Rust and reach 100% test parity."<br/>3. "Improve application scaffolding to get the largest contentful paint in production to below 2.5s."<br/>\*The prompt doesn’t always have to be a number but generally it helps with the next tips.<br/>If you are unsure how to best define your goal or you want to work with Codex first to brainstorm the project you don’t have to start a thread with goal mode.<br/>Codex can set a goal on its own so you can start a conversation and when you are ready for Codex to start the work you can ask Codex to set the goal based on your conversation.<br/>You can also always edit the goal at any point in time by pressing the edit button in the Codex app or using /goal again in the CLI.<br/>## <br/>2\. Provide guidance if possible<br/>Sending a prompt like "Reduce the build and deployment time by 30%" can be cool and even find some creative solutions. It could also send Codex down a wild goose chase if you have an idea where the issue might lie.<br/>When possible give Codex a starting point where to start working, what tools it can use to achieve the goal, or any other pointers where Codex might go down the wrong path.<br/>My colleague <br/>[@reach\_v</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 1,018 · 🔁 72 · 💬 26 · 🔖 2,268</p><p><a href="https://x.com/dkundel/status/2062650378089594955">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
