      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Agno</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/AgnoAgi">@AgnoAgi</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062248271444111360">http://x.com/i/article/2062248271444111360</a></p></blockquote><div><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ1HCcPX0AEHjMH.jpg" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/></div><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062248271444111360">http://x.com/i/article/2062248271444111360</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2062248271444111360/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>Did someone say … cookies?<br/>X and its partners use cookies to provide you with a better, safer and faster service and to support our business. Some cookies are necessary to use our services, improve our services, and make sure they work properly. Show more about your choices.<br/>Accept all cookies<br/>Refuse non-essential cookies<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ6VxovWYAA3JlG?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2062248271444111360/AgnoAgi/article/2062255866724884708/media/2062250359364411392)<br/>Community Roundup: May 2026 <br/>[![Square profile picture](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1984361332624306176/KaNuKvU4_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2062248271444111360/AgnoAgi)<br/>[Agno](http://x.com/i/article/2062248271444111360/AgnoAgi)<br/>[@AgnoAgi](http://x.com/i/article/2062248271444111360/AgnoAgi)<br/>·<br/>18h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow AgnoAgi<br/>5<br/>12<br/>[1K](http://x.com/i/article/2062248271444111360/AgnoAgi/status/2062255866724884708/analytics)<br/>We were announced as <br/>[@GoogleDeepMind](https://x.com/@GoogleDeepMind)<br/> ecosystem partners with at Google I/O. 40,000 GitHub stars. v2.6.0 through v2.6.8\. Agents earning USDC. Agents living in Matrix rooms. Agents managing someone's grocery inventory from their Apple Watch.<br/>May was a milestone month. Here's what happened.<br/>40,000 GitHub stars<br/>Easy to wave off as a vanity metric. But behind this number are thousands of people filing bugs, opening PRs, and putting Agno into real projects. That's the part that matters. Thank you.<br/>What shipped in v2.6.0 through v2.6.8<br/>Context Providers: the headline of v2.6.0\. A first-class API for plugging an external source into an agent as a natural-language tool. Filesystem, web, SQL database, Slack, Google Drive, or any MCP server. Attach a provider and the agent reasons over it directly. No hand-rolled retrieval pipelines.<br/>Multi-framework support in AgentOS: AgentOS now runs Claude SDK, LangGraph, and DSPy agents alongside Agno under one operational surface. One runtime. Multiple frameworks. No second stack.<br/>Team HITL and Approvals: human-in-the-loop graduated to teams in v2.6.0 with a full API layer wired into the AgentOS chat page. Background runs over SSE can now be reconnected and resumed, so a refresh mid-run picks up where you left off.<br/>Workspace Tools: safe local filesystem access for agents. Read, list, search, write, edit, move, delete, and shell access to a root directory tree. Destructive operations gated behind HITL confirmation by default. The right way to let an agent work on a project on disk.<br/>Claude prompt caching, multi-block: per-block cache and TTL controls, a cache\_tools flag, and deterministic tool ordering so request prefixes stay stable and caches actually hit.<br/>Also shipped: WorkspaceContextProvider, Gmail and Calendar context providers, GDrive OAuth support, Slack multi-row approvals, per-user data isolation in AgentOS, Gemini multimodal file search, Gemini Interactions, and first-party Google Antigravity support.<br/>Community projects<br/>Harish Kotra built a Secure Playground: an interactive prompt-injection attack and defense simulator with Agno evaluator agents scoring attacks and defenses in real time.<br/>Bas Nijholt built MindRoom: AI agents living in Matrix rooms, remembering context, using tools, and working across bridged Discord, Slack, and WhatsApp chats. Multi-agent, multi-user, and federated by design.<br/>Alexandre built AgnoLab: a visual canvas for building and orchestrating Agno agents. Watch workflows run as you build them.<br/>Gagan Dasari built a personal life-management agent that reads grocery receipts to update pantry inventory, pulls Apple Watch data to log workouts, and creates custom Notion views to track gym progress and spending.<br/>Eliottre built TaskBounty: a marketplace where autonomous agents compete on real tasks and get paid in USDC, ETH,</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 14 · 🔁 5 · 💬 1 · 🔖 5</p><p><a href="https://x.com/AgnoAgi/status/2062255866724884708">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
