## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ545MEXEAAc0o3?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/saameeey/article/2062229308878581772/media/2062218603269656576) The AI Integration Layer Is Becoming the New Backend...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Samuel Umoren</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/saameeey">@saameeey</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112">http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112">http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ545MEXEAAc0o3?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/saameeey/article/2062229308878581772/media/2062218603269656576)<br/>The AI Integration Layer Is Becoming the New Backend <br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2054193751174598656/2HFrpykx_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/saameeey)<br/>[Samuel Umoren](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/saameeey)<br/>[@saameeey](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/saameeey)<br/>·<br/>13h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow saameeey<br/>4<br/>3<br/>25<br/>[2.9K](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/saameeey/status/2062229308878581772/analytics)<br/>Backend development has always been the part of software where product behavior becomes enforceable.<br/>The backend manages identity, permissions, data storage, business logic, background jobs, APIs, and third-party integrations. It is where product rules become systems that customers can actually use.<br/>With AI products, that baseline stays in place.<br/>The added backend work sits around the LLM and the agent using it.<br/>An AI product has to retrieve the right customer context, preserve source permissions, decide which tools an agent can use, execute those tool calls safely, route requests across models, track cost, log what happened, and give teams a way to audit the system.<br/>That sounds like a lot, right? Yes, it is. This work lives between the product, the LLM, the agent, and the customer's business systems. Let's call it the AI integration layer.<br/>You can describe the underlying architecture in three paths:<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ55QySWwAAoEeW?format=png&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/saameeey/article/2062229308878581772/media/2062219008665894912)<br/>The three paths of the AI integration layer<br/>In this piece, i'll be referencing <br/>[Merge.dev](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112//Merge.dev)<br/>. <br/>[@merge\_api](https://x.com/@merge%5Fapi)<br/> builds integration infrastructure for companies that need to connect their products to customer systems. Its recent product direction extends that work into AI infrastructure: <br/>[Unified](https://www.merge.dev/blog/the-new-merge)<br/> handles synced business context, <br/>[Agent Handler ](https://docs.merge.dev/merge-agent-handler/overview)<br/>handles governed tool execution, and <br/>[Gateway](https://docs.merge.dev/merge-gateway/features/routing-policies/overview)<br/> handles model routing, observability, and control.<br/>Put differently, the integration layer is becoming the backend around the LLM.<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ55bpNXoAA5WsW?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/saameeey/article/2062229308878581772/media/2062219195207622656)<br/>Traditional backend responsibilities beside AI backend additions<br/>## <br/>AI products add a second backend surface<br/>A traditional SaaS backend usually has a familiar set of responsibilities:<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ6AeN_WwAA57hA?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/saameeey/article/2062229308878581772/media/2062226936022089728)<br/>When a product adds AI capabilities, these responsibilities remain.<br/>Then the AI layer introduces another set of runtime responsibilities:<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ6AoWyWwAAXabF?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/i/article/2062217540411994112/saameeey/article/2062229308878581772/media/2062227110182174720)<br/>AI products need these responsibilities because they interact with customer systems differently from traditional applications.<br/>A traditional app usually exposes a workflow through screens, forms, buttons, and API calls. The user performs the action, and then the backend validates it, writes data, and records the result.<br/>With agents, the workflow is compressed because the agent reads context, ch</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 40 · 🔁 6 · 💬 5 · 🔖 67</p><p><a href="https://x.com/saameeey/status/2062229308878581772">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>@libapi_: Hermes Studio 0.6.10 版本更新 - 辅助模型 辅助模型可以理解成 Hermes Studio 里的“后台小助手”。...</title>
      <link>https://x.com/libapi_/status/2062380163338535064</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">2062380163338535064</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 04 Jun 2026 03:45:22 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>libapi</dc:creator>
      <description>Hermes Studio 0.6.10 版本更新 - 辅助模型
&gt;
&gt; 辅助模型可以理解成 Hermes Studio 里的“后台小助手”。
&gt;
&gt; 它不一定直接参与聊天，但会负责一些幕后任务，比如压缩聊天上下文、处理视觉内容、网页提取、审批、MCP 调用、标题生成等。
&gt;
&gt; 以前这些任务通常会跟着当前正在聊天的模型走；现在你可以给每个配置文件单独指定一个更合适的 Provider 和模型。
&gt;
&gt; 比如：聊天本身用一个强模型，而上下文压缩交给一个更快、更便宜的模型；视觉任务也可以单独换成更擅长看图的模型。
&gt;
&gt; 这样做的好处是：主聊天模型可以专心负责对话，辅助任务则交给更适合的模型来处理，整体会更灵活，也更容易控制速度、成本和效果。
&gt;
&gt; 另外，现在也可以直接在界面里刷新 Provider 的模型目录，不用手动重启或改配置，点一下就能拉到最新的模型列表。

