      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>DuckDB</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/duckdb">@duckdb</a>)</p><blockquote><p>🔗 <a href="https://duckdb.org/library/duckdb-not-quack-science/">https://duckdb.org/library/duckdb-not-quack-science/</a></p></blockquote><div><img src="https://duckdb.org/images/sharingduckdb.jpg" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://duckdb.org/images/logo-dl/DuckDB_Logo-horizontal.svg" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://duckdb.org/images/blog/authors/gabor_szarnyas.png" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://duckdb.org/images/library/thumbs/placeholder-duckdb-2.svg" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://duckdb.org/images/library/thumbs/placeholder-duckdb-1.svg" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ3wBHzW8AAR0Em.jpg" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/></div><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="https://duckdb.org/library/duckdb-not-quack-science/">DuckDB: Not Quack Science – DuckDB</a></p><blockquote>Documentation Getting Started Installation Quack Remote Protocol Guides Data Import Client APIs SQL Introduction Why DuckDB Resources Blog Library Events Everywhere Webshop Design FAQ GitHub 38.6k Support Support DuckDB: Not Quack Science Gábor Szárnyas 2026-05-27 · 35 min Event Ubuntu Summit 2026 Slides Download YouTube DuckDB: Not Quack Science Abstract DuckDB is an open-source SQL database system, geared towards analytical workloads. DuckDB ships a state-of-the-art database architecture as a single package, that is available both as a command line tool and as an in-process library. Uniquely among databases, DuckDB focuses on user experience and portability, making it easy to set up almost anywhere. In this talk, I give a high-level overview of DuckDB. I explain our “friendly SQL” language, which builds on Postgres’ SQL dialect and makes it more ergonomic while staying backwards-compatible. I also present our “friendly CLI”, a command line interface optimized for productivity. I show case studies on how you can process hundreds of GBs of data on your laptop or tens of terabytes on a single server. Other Library Resources DuckCon #7 Talk 30 min DuckCon #7 – State of the Duck 2026-06-24 Hannes Mühleisen and Mark Raasveldt infoq.com Paper DuckDB Quack: Client/Server Protocol over HTTP for Multi-User Analytics 2026-05-31 Renato Losio (InfoQ) Joe Reis Podcast 70 min Quack w/ Hannes Mühleisen 2026-05-28 Hannes Mühleisen All library resources DuckDB is an open-source project by DuckLabs . Documentation Getting Started Installation Guides Data Import Client APIs SQL Introduction Quack Remote Protocol Why DuckDB Resources Engineering Blog Library Quack Page Events Webshop RSS Feed Status Page FAQ Development Release Calendar Roadmap Building DuckDB GitHub Issues Related Sites DuckLake DuckLabs DuckDB Foundation Commercial Support Community Community Extensions LinkedIn Bluesky X (Twitter) Discord © 2026 DuckDB Foundation, Amsterdam NL Code of Conduct Trademark Use</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 3 · 🔁 1 · 🔖 5</p><p><a href="https://x.com/duckdb/status/2062070251848638815">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
